<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl pb-16 pt-8 text-zinc-700">
  <section class="rounded-3xl border border-zinc-200 bg-[#faf8f5] px-6 py-12 text-center sm:px-10">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#8f2c00]">About YouCongress</p>
    <h1 class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 sm:text-5xl">
      Public positions you can inspect, challenge, and reuse
    </h1>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">
      YouCongress is a non-profit, open-source, open-data project that turns public statements
      into traceable records connected to specific claims and policy proposals. The first large
      focus is AI governance, safety, jobs, and society.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-900 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-zinc-700"
      >
        Explore sourced positions
      </a>
      <a
        href="/dataset"
        class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-300 bg-white px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-zinc-900 hover:border-zinc-500"
      >
        Download the data
      </a>
      <a
        :if={@ai_policy_launch?}
        href="/ai"
        class="rounded-lg border border-[#d96b39] bg-white px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-brand hover:bg-[#fbeee7]"
      >
        100 AI Policies initiative
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="rounded-2xl border border-indigo-100 bg-white p-7 shadow-sm">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-600">Evidence layer</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-900">Who said what, with sources</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        We preserve the quotation, author, source, publication date, linked claim or proposal,
        and the stance inferred for that precise relationship. Verification histories keep source
        fidelity, relevance, and stance checks separate.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-white p-7 shadow-sm">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-700">
          Participation layer
        </p>
        <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-700 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-white">
          beta
        </span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-900">Direct votes and optional delegation</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        Citizens can vote directly, add their reasoning, or delegate to people they trust.
        Direct participant votes are different from stances inferred from public statements and
        should be interpreted separately.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-900 px-6 py-10 text-white sm:px-10">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#f0a882]">
      Read this before using the data
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold">What YouCongress does not claim</h2>
    <div class="mt-7 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-800 p-5">
        <h3 class="font-bold">Not a representative poll</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
          The corpus reflects its sources, searches, contributors, and time periods. More records
          on one side do not show that more experts or citizens hold that view.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-800 p-5">
        <h3 class="font-bold">Not a truth or expertise score</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
          A stance label describes how a passage bears on a statement. It does not measure whether
          the passage is correct or how much evidential weight its speaker deserves.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-800 p-5">
        <h3 class="font-bold">AI verification is not human validation</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
          “AI Verified” means an automated verifier found support for an annotation. Agreement
          among automated passes is not independent evidence.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-800 p-5">
        <h3 class="font-bold">Correlation remains visible work</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
          Several quotations may come from one hearing, report, or event. Record counts should not
          be treated as independent observations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#8f2c00]">
      How a record is built
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-900">
      Provenance first, annotations second
    </h2>
    <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 p-5">
        <p class="font-bold text-zinc-900">
          <span class="mr-3 text-brand">01</span>Discover and preserve
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Find the original source and keep the attributable passage, date, and author together.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 p-5">
        <p class="font-bold text-zinc-900">
          <span class="mr-3 text-brand">02</span>Connect carefully
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Link the passage only to claims or proposals it directly addresses or substantially bears on.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 p-5">
        <p class="font-bold text-zinc-900">
          <span class="mr-3 text-brand">03</span>Classify the relationship
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Annotate whether the passage supports, opposes, or remains unclear about each linked statement.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 p-5">
        <p class="font-bold text-zinc-900">
          <span class="mr-3 text-brand">04</span>Verify and correct
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Check authenticity, relevance, and stance separately while preserving corrections and review history.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed">
      Read the detailed
      <a href="/faq#verify-quotes" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">
        verification guide
      </a>
      or inspect the <a
        href="https://github.com/youcongress/youcongress"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline"
      >open-source workflow</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14 grid gap-8 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-14 md:grid-cols-[.85fr_1.15fr]">
    <div>
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#8f2c00]">Who is behind it</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-900">Named people, public work</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-5 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        YouCongress was started by <a
          href="https://hecperez.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline"
        >Hector Perez</a>,
        an AI engineering leader in Madrid who has worked on liquid-democracy and civic-knowledge
        projects since 2008, including AgreeList and Notes.club.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a
          href="https://www.gonzalocardenete.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline"
        >
          Gonzalo Cardenete
        </a>
        contributes UX and design experience, including earlier work on the Decidim open-source
        participation platform at Barcelona City Council.
      </p>
      <p>
        We welcome criticism and corrections. Email
        <a href="mailto:hello@youcongress.org" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">
          hello@youcongress.org
        </a>
        or use the report links attached to public records.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-[#faf8f5] p-7 sm:p-9">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#8f2c00]">Open by design</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-900">Reusable public infrastructure</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed">
      Application code is licensed under MIT. Structured annotations and metadata are released
      under CC BY 4.0; quoted third-party material and author biographies remain subject to their
      original rights holders. Records are available through the public website, CSV exports, and
      a no-key MCP endpoint for compatible research tools.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a
        href="/dataset"
        class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-900 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-zinc-700"
      >
        Dataset and licenses
      </a>
      <a
        href="/mcp-tools"
        class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-300 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 hover:border-zinc-500"
      >
        Research-tool access
      </a>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-300 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 hover:border-zinc-500"
      >
        Contact us
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
